+        <b>Pattern #1:</b> The entire diagnostic report (as created by the fulfiller of the order(s)) is represented by a bundle containing <b>one</b> DiagnosticReport resource for the patient for a particular point in time. Some concepts, such as panels, are always represented as Observations, where <code>Observation.code</code> equals the panel code, and <code>Observation.organizer</code> is <code>true</code>.
     </p>
     <p>
         In the case of laboratory reports, the <code>DiagnosticReport.code</code> names the report type (e.g. "Pathology Report"). The <code>DiagnosticReport.result</code> element references at least one Observation that can act as an organizer (grouper) for tests commonly performed together, often referred to as a "panel" or "battery". In this organizer, <code>Observation.code</code> names the panel (e.g. "CBC"), <code>Observation.value[x]</code> is not present, and <code>Observation.hasMember</code> lists all the Observation resources that are grouped by it. To clearly indicate this as an organizer, <code>Observation.organizer</code> is set to <code>true</code>. This supports multiple top-level panels or batteries under an instance of a DiagnosticReport.
     </p>
